# Nest + LQ scaffold

When adding HTTP endpoints, services, controllers, DTOs, or use-case folders in a project that has `src/core/`:

1. Load the `lq-nest-scaffold` skill (or follow its workflow).
2. Prefer `lq service <kebab-name> --module <module> --http <Method> --no-interactive` over creating boilerplate files by hand.
3. Use `--dry-run --format=json` first when planning file paths.
4. After generation, register providers/controllers in the Nest `*.module.ts`.

Do not duplicate DDD folder structures without CLI flags (`--cqrs`, `--domain`, `--type resource`).

CLI docs live in the `lq-cqrs-cli` repository: `docs/commands.md`.
